","updated_at":"2026-06-22T14:36:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduced in 4.6 Forward+ and Mobile.\nNot reproduced in 4.6 Compatibility.\nNot reproduced in 4.5.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10, AMD PRO A10-8700B R6, 4 core, AMD Radeon R6, 64 bit system, D3D12 (i think).\n\n### Issue description\n\nLoading up new projects with Forward+ or Mobile on 4.6 causes either permanent unresponsiveness (white screen), or loading a complete black screen when loading.\nIssue not reproduceable on compatibility or 4.5's Forward+.\nRunning ported projects from 4.5 gives this in 3D view, no issues in 2D.\n\n<img width=\"751\" height=\"525\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d08be0b-c840-4bda-94f1-b5a287eb6ff5\" />\n\nAttempted to run with verbose, got a strange glitched screen and the following errors.\n<img width=\"716\" height=\"476\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f42cf3a-3037-4e9e-ba7c-38c1982b1328\" />\n\n<img width=\"742\" height=\"244\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/77965119-8823-4c73-b657-0dd081c827fe\" />\nLoading in mobile gives this sometimes, and a similar error to the one above some other times.\n\n<img width=\"906\" height=\"206\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3008a257-f587-4084-a4c1-82c1af7038b1\" />\n\nProbably related to DX12, unsure of why and why turning off fallback to DX12 doesn't affect the issue.\n\n\n**To summarize, Forward+ and Mobile keep choosing D3D12 forcibly regardless of any settings or even startup commands, as visible in the cmd panel + verbose setting, it subsequently fails at running D3D12 correctly.**\n\nTo be clear, D3D12 and related dlls are installed on the system (version 10.0.19041.5794), and D3D12 using games run perfectly okay.\nTo be clear 2, the projects run fine in compatibility and run fine in 4.5, 4.6 seems to have changed priority to D3D12 while also not being able to run D3D12 perfectly on all devices (somehow?), I was able to change different renderers by loading into an old, ported project from 4.5 which still ran even with the bug above.\n\nTo be clear 3, Not to be confused with the other major D3D12 rendering issue [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/95619), which causes the popups to glitch weirdly, here it causes a crash when booting.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nBoot up an entirely new project with 4.6, toggling off DX12 fallback does nothing, unsure of other factors that cause the problem.\nYou can boot up an old ported project with a visual bug in the 3D view.\nThis is not reproducible on all devices, but some other devices have had this issue.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115588/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null}